API-15: return the roughness error from a pipe's EN_SETTING

For a pipe, EN_setlinkvalue(EN_INITSETTING or EN_SETTING) calls itself
with EN_ROUGHNESS, but discarded the return code. A roughness of 0 or
less was refused, nothing changed, and the caller got 0. Return the
error code of the roughness assignment.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-15_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..838f77d 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -4224,7 +4224,8 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setlinkvalue(EN_Project p, int index, int property, double valu
     case EN_SETTING:
         if (Link[index].Type == PIPE || Link[index].Type == CVPIPE)
         {
-            EN_setlinkvalue(p, index, EN_ROUGHNESS, value);
+            int errcode = EN_setlinkvalue(p, index, EN_ROUGHNESS, value);
+            if (errcode > 0) return errcode;
             if (property == EN_INITSETTING) Link[index].InitSetting = Link[index].Kc;
         }
         else
